text:
Felix: Heads-up from mobile QA: when the left rail collapses on small phones the job list loses a few pixels at the bottom and action menus can get covered. Repro: Console -> Jobs -> narrow width ~360px -> toggle rail. Screenshot: https://internal/screens/rail-clip-360.png

Jun: Got it. Is the clip during the toggle animation or once it's settled?

Felix: During the animation. It looks like our container height recalcs (100vh issue) while the address bar hides, so rows shift. The popover overlay also sits underneath the rail overlay.

Tara: Likely two separate fixes: avoid relying on 100vh (use visualViewport or CSS env) and portal the row popovers to a root layer so they aren't constrained by rail transforms.

Oren: Agreed. Quick patch idea: add padding-bottom: env(safe-area-inset-bottom) to list container and switch animations to translateX on the rail only. But transforms create stacking contexts, so popovers must live at body level.

Priya: Accessibility: when the rail becomes an overlay we need aria-hidden on main content and focus trapped to the rail. Also change the toggle label to "Open navigation" / "Close navigation" for SR clarity. Disable tooltips on touch.

Felix: Small CSS I tried locally to reduce clipping:```css
@media (max-width:440px){
  .rail{position:fixed;top:var(--header-h);bottom:0;left:0;width:240px;transform:translateX(-100%);}  
  .rail.open{transform:translateX(0)}
  .list{padding-bottom:env(safe-area-inset-bottom)}
}
```

Jun: That helps but remember transform -> stacking context. Portaling popovers to body + position:fixed is the robust fix; compute popover coords with getBoundingClientRect. Respect prefers-reduced-motion.

Oren: UX question: should we use a two-step breakpoint (icons-only then overlay) or a single switch? I prefer icons-only between 460-520 and overlay <=459 to avoid width thrash on narrow tablets.

Tara: Two-step sounds good. If we do that, keep CSS vars for thresholds so Product can tweak without deployments. Also ensure icon-only still provides 44px touch targets.

Priya: Copy nit: use "Open navigation" on the small toggle, and for row action toggles use "Row actions" tooltip but disable on touch. Also auto-close open row menus when the rail toggles.

Felix: I'll prototype overlay+portal+aria changes in the sandbox and attach variants for 360/412/480 widths. Can we pick final thresholds by Friday? @Jun @Oren

Jun: I'll run visual diffs across device matrix and test popover z-order. Aim for a PR by Thu.

